WEBVTT

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.840
Hey! Are you guys adventurers?!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.660
Yes. We're on our way 
to a dungeon!

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.620
Awesome! Good luck!

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.940
Leaving the capital on a journey 
is rather exciting!

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.750
Don't forget. 
We aren't out here for fun.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.630
We're investigating the dragon's vein.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.160
Y-Yes! Of course we are.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.600
And our current destination 
is the Melkia Dungeon.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.960
I've heard that Melkia is an enormous dungeon 
having hundreds of floors.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.940
But dungeon cities are pretty safe, 
so I'm sure we'll be fine!

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.850
"Dungeon cities"?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.380
Y-Yes!

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.340
There's a city built over the dungeon.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.360
A city?!

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.450
Yes?

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.850
<i>There was nothing like that 
in my past life.</i>

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.910
<i>People can live on top 
of a dungeon that dangerous?</i>

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.050
This sounds pretty neat!

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.620
It's a town of adventurers!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.500
I'm sure it'll be brimming with life!

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.530
It will take several days 
to reach Melkia.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:10.000
Let's take our time.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.800
What? It's not far. 
We can reach it in a day.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.380
But...

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.300
We'll arrive by tonight!

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.370
Do you mean...

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:24.460
You want to pass 
through the Forest of Chikirisubia?

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.730
But it's a monster den!

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:27.800
Yeah!

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.980
And it's not just strong monsters...

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.320
Rumors say there's a really smart monster 
showing up lately.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.690
A smart monster?

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.220
Oh, no!

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.990
We got him curious!

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.960
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.960
<b>The Strongest Sage Goes on a Journey.</b>

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.460
It's awfully unsettling in here, isn't it?

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.810
I can always fly you guys out 
if it comes to that.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.830
Your wings are still healing, remember?

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.650
Oh, I forgot.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.880
I'm beat!

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.580
Strange that we're not seeing 
many monsters, though.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.240
I prefer that to the alternative.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.390
But I'm so hungry!

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.950
I'm sure you are. 
Let's have lunch!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.300
Great idea!

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:53.000
Let's pull some rations 
from our storage spe—

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.300
No. Let's find our food here.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.250
I'll hunt us up something.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.720
Countless monsters' magic signatures,

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.700
but they're moving 
in a conspicuously orderly fashion.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.980
Someone's commanding them.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.980
There's one intentionally restrained 
magic signature among them.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.940
That must be

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.780
the smart monster!

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.560
I-Is that...

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.130
C-Can it be...

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.830
I'm hungry!

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.770
I was disappointed, to be frank.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.170
It doesn't look very yummy.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.720
It's a Wism Monkey!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.980
It's a famously smart monster.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.390
Then the monster everyone's talking about...

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.240
It's probably this, yeah.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.560
But forget about that.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.520
More importantly...

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.260
Oh, step back!

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.360
Well, Iris?

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.860
This one looks better, right?

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.820
Yes!

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.920
Hang on! 
Are we gonna eat that?!

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.580
Is it even possible to eat monsters?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.100
Not all of them, of course,

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.790
but this one's just fine.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.830
It's kind of a delicacy, really.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.790
If you say so...

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.090
Really? Are you being serious?!

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.530
Now, let's get it cooked up!

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.010
Of course. Let me start...

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.680
I see.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.880
Refining iron from the ground 
to make a pot.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.350
Yes! We'll forage for our tools as well!

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.810
I'm gonna forage, too!

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.000
I'll prepare the firewood!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.780
Then I'll gather up some local plants 
to make a soup!

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.610
I think that's enough, Iris.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.030
You think?

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.520
What did you just do?!

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:01.710
I don't usually have trouble with fire spells,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.920
but for some reason, 
having the ingredients nearby makes it blow up.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:10.700
I can still handle the cooking part! 
I can!

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.480
You don't believe me? 
But I really can!

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.560
Say something, Lurie!

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.920
I-It looks tasty enough...

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.660
It's quite ample...

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.040
So good!

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.580
Alma's special soup!

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:43.040
It might be a little 
on the strong side, of course!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.540
I've never seen you cook before!

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.020
I was banned from the kitchen back home!

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.470
I'm not picky!

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:02.230
Not even a darkness dragon can tolerate it?

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.840
Alma, what in the world 
did you put in there?

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:07.480
I made it the normal way! Sheesh!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:10.190
I could stand to eat a lot more,

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:13.870
but I suppose this human body 
is around 80% full.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.780
After eating all that?

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.940
You have quite an appetite!

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:21.230
Were you that desperate 
to cancel out the taste of the soup?

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.330
That again? Really?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.160
Well, let's get going.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:30.580
I think the forest monsters 
are too afraid of Iris to approach.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.230
Dragon magic power! Is that why?

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:37.060
Plus he beat the Wism Monkey, 
which is probably an incentive to stay away.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.760
Yeah.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.980
We'll reach Melkia before sundown.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.220
We're here!

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:01.500
So this is dungeon city Melkia...

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.130
What is all this?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:11.580
I expected a little more life 
in a dungeon city.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.420
But it seems far more bleak 
than the capital.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.270
What's that?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.640
A magic lamppost?

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.580
Yes, but there's something strange 
about how the magic flows.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.560
You typically power magic equipment 
with magistones,

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:32.620
but this one seems directly tapped 
into the dragon's vein.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:35.410
And in a slapdash fashion, at that.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.780
If it's left like this—

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.780
Hey!

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.810
It's not safe there!

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.540
Those things explode sometimes.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.160
At least ten people have died this year alone.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.120
Not good!

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.130
Get away, all of you!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.840
Why would you make something 
so dangerous?!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.460
H-Hang on! Calm down!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:00.680
We don't have a choice. 
It's was on the lord's orders.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.180
We used to use magistones.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:07.900
But our lord said that magistones
are our most precious export,

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.600
so he forbids us from using them.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.930
How awful!

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.250
What could your new lord be thinking?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.320
Yeah! 
Setting up dangerous stuff like that...

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:23.660
Is the lord also the reason 
why you're so underpopulated?

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.390
Yeah, apparently a powerful monster 
has appeared

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.470
around the tenth floor 
of the dungeon.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:33.120
Most of the adventurers were sent in 
on the lord's orders.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.820
Veteran and greenhorn alike.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:38.220
I see. So that's the reason.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.680
Can I have one for each of us?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.310
S-Sure...

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.880
The local lord sounds like a creep!

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.180
I feel for the poor townspeople!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:51.220
He appears quite incompetent.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:54.720
If you send a lot of inexperienced people 
on a monster hunt,

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.400
they'll just trip each other up.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.620
The area's weapons seem to be 
of poor quality as well.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.980
What will we do next?

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.630
Let's head to the guild first.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:12.420
"To enter the dungeon, 
you need a guild-issued permit," it says.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:16.380
I want to enter the dungeon 
and have a look for ourselves.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.710
Excuse me!

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:23.450
I'd like a permit to enter the dungeon.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.000
A permit?

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.960
I would advise against that.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.270
Why? What's wrong with it?

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:33.740
The permits aren't issued by the guild, 
but by the lord himself.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.010
So as long as you stay in Melkia,

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:39.660
you have to participate 
in any special requests the lord asks of you.

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:44.670
<i>So to get a permit, 
we have to serve as the lord's lapdogs.</i>

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:47.290
Are those special requests 
typically dangerous?

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:52.230
They come in many forms, 
from dungeon exploration to monster hunting,

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:54.920
but they're uniformly absurd.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:59.100
They come about once a month, 
but every one results in casualties.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.270
Children like you could never—

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:02.640
I should ask just in case.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.360
What do you want to do?

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.580
I'm totally in!

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.720
I'll follow you anywhere, Matty!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.430
Me, too!

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.850
Listen to these brats run their mouths!

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.480
You see what that dungeon did 
to adults like us?

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.580
I'd like four permits, please.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:20.780
Very well. 
We can start the application process.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.940
We have a huge number of injuries 
from a monster attack!

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:26.330
There are too many injured 
for us to keep up!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.790
Does anyone know healing spells?

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:33.060
All the real adventurers are in the dungeon!

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.600
You really think—

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:35.760
There's one right here.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.800
Matty...

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.970
Take me where I need to go.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.890
We're out of bandages! Bring some new ones!

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:48.890
This is...

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:53.020
I can't stop the bleeding! 
I need healing spells, fast!

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.100
I'm locked down here.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.480
I need help!

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.350
This is awful...

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:58.190
Look at that.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.500
They can't even manage a stopgap.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.650
In a dungeon city full of adventurers...

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.010
Why do they have so few healers?

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:07.280
We used to have a number on staff,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.620
but they were all driven out by the lord.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.440
He said they were a waste of money!

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.080
It's wrong to let people die 
due to the orders of an incompetent lord.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:20.090
I will save them all!

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.740
<i>I'll start with a Passive Detect.</i>

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:26.940
<i>I'll feel out the patients' magic power 
to get a quick idea of their status.</i>

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.310
These numbers represent 
their injuries' severity.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.430
I'll look at the worst off among them.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:39.180
The rest of you, cast healing spells 
in descending order of urgency.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.230
We will!

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:43.800
Hold it!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.950
You can't just barge in here like this!

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.900
People's lives are on the line!

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.840
This is no place for children!

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:52.700
Can you save them all by yourself?

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.500
Of course not!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.540
I have to triage them 
based on their condition

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.600
to keep losses to a minimum!

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.800
Then be quiet and watch.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.300
Typical nonsense, 
from a Crest of Failure!

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:10.440
Actually, this kind of healing is the sort 
that the Crest of Failure is best at.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.620
Close the blood vessels 
to stanch the bleeding.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.770
Heal the damaged organs.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.600
Then close the wound!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.880
Success.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.030
Th-Thank you...

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.770
You healed him. 
From such a severe wound...

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:29.790
The wound's completely gone!

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.260
I'm asking you again.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.660
Cast your healing spells 
in the order on the tablets.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.210
If we all work together, 
we can save them all.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.870
V-Very well.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:42.590
Split up and cast those spells!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.830
Sir!

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.680
Lurie, 23's okay!

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:48.930
Move on to the next patient!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:49.840
Right!

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.640
Recovery on 27's not going fast enough!

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:53.900
Come with me, you two!

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:55.600
All right, we'll do it!

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.900
I'm... done for...

00:13:58.900 --> 00:13:59.980
Don't give up!

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.270
We will save you!

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.770
W-We'll help, too!

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:06.350
Do your best!

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:08.230
Hey, speak to me!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.280
It's all done!

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.620
Healing successful on everyone.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:24.200
I can't believe we really saved them all...

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:29.010
Despite looking like a child, 
are you a famous healer, by chance?

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.240
Certainly not.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.530
I've actually used healing 
only magic a few times.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.350
But you orchestrated this miracle...

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.340
"Miracle"?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:42.690
No, as I said before, 
this was the act of everyone here.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.400
I haven't properly thanked you yet.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.280
Thank you. Truly.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.410
Same to you.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:51.700
Oh, there is one thing I wanted to ask...

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:52.820
What is it?

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.040
The previous lord.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.670
Why was he replaced?

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.290
Did he pass away, by chance?

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:03.880
<i>From what I've heard, 
the previous lord knew what he was doing.</i>

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.320
<i>If he really got replaced 
with a complete incompetent...</i>

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.580
Yes, and without warning.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.510
He passed away abruptly in his sleep.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.360
Was he ill?

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.220
We simply don't know.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:19.570
An abrupt, unexplained death...

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:23.690
That was all we could ascertain.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.560
<i>Dungeons were considered dangerous 
even in my old life.</i>

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.550
<i>To build a city over one...</i>

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.810
<i>I thought it was unusual from the start.</i>

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:35.900
<i>This world has been altered by demons.</i>

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:39.290
<i>This must be another example 
of that in progress.</i>

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:43.260
<i>The demons must have killed 
the previous lord.</i>

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:46.380
<i>There's a chance 
that the current lord is a demon himself.</i>

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.580
<i>I'll have to meet him and find out.</i>

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.860
Zoom!

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:56.810
I must say... 
The current lord is quite cruel!

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.160
We have to do something!

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.390
Agreed!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.550
I agree.

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.730
That's why I'm writing 
the headmaster a letter.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:07.600
I see! You're going to have him 
forward it to the king?

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:08.790
Exactly.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.940
This is what I went with.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.500
"We don't know 
what the homework is while we're here."

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.740
"May we be excused from it?"

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.400
What in the world?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:19.880
It's a decoy, of course.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.040
This is the real one.

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:25.320
I'll hide it under a false bottom 
in the delivery box.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:29.000
Obviously, I've use magic 
to make it harder to spot.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:33.220
I worked out this method of correspondence 
with the headmaster in advance.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.420
Protection against inspection?

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:38.130
And they must be inspecting the mail,

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:41.890
or the capital would have heard 
about what's going on in Melkia earlier.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.350
Precisely.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:46.170
This will help us avoid the inspection.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:49.300
Wouldn't it be faster 
if you went there personally?

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:50.690
Most likely,

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.270
but I want to see what's going on 
in the dungeon first.

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:55.660
We got our permits, after all.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.490
The dungeon, huh?

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:01.100
It's got that monster 
that hurt all the people today, right?

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:02.550
Are you sure about this?

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:05.990
If we leave it at large, 
it might reach the surface!

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:06.670
Exactly.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.900
Let's check it out tomorrow.

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:11.640
For today, let's all have a nice rest.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:27.650
<i>I just realized I'm spending the night 
in the same building as Matty...</i>

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.960
<i>And the same room, at that!</i>

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:32.470
<i>I even let him see me in my pajamas!</i>

00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:34.610
<i>It's so, so, so bad!</i>

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.850
<i>This is my first time 
spending the night with Lurie,</i>

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:41.790
<i>though Alma and Iris are here, too.</i>

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:44.300
<i>Just get your mind off it, man!</i>

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:46.200
<i>She just happens to be 
in the next bed over!</i>

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.610
<i>She just happens...</i>

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:49.880
Let's bust in there!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:53.000
Leave it all to me...

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:53.800
<i>She's talking in her sleep?</i>

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.510
<i>Don't startle me like that!</i>

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.970
C'mon... Drink more...

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:01.550
Can't... I'm sorry...

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.550
<i>They're talking to each other?!</i>

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.060
<i>Why are they in sync?!</i>

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.320
<i>Just calm down.</i>

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.460
<i>You've had a long day, 
and you're tired.</i>

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:11.980
<i>Just close your eyes, 
and before you know it...</i>

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.630
<i>Remain calm. Calm.</i>

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.510
<i>Sleep as you always do, 
in preparation for tomorrow.</i>

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.630
<i>I still can't sleep!</i>

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:25.840
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.610
<i>I have to find a way to sleep.</i>

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:29.600
<i>That's it.</i>

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.640
<i>Let's count monsters until I sleep.</i>

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.980
<i>One monster.</i>

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:35.040
<i>Two monsters.</i>

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.080
<i>Three monsters.</i>

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.320
<i>Four monsters.</i>

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.270
<i>Five monsters.</i>

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:39.860
<i>Six monsters.</i>

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:49.580
You almost used Dragon's Breath 
in your sleep earlier.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:51.560
You could've blown the whole inn away.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:53.810
I'll be more careful.

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:56.530
Why do you look so sleepy 
when you slept all night?

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.990
Boy, isn't morning air the best?

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:03.600
Right, Lurie?

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:06.430
Are you okay? 
Did you get any sleep?

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:07.660
Absolutely.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.420
<i>You liar.</i>

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.000
This is the dungeon gate?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.590
It's so big!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:17.340
But it's just iron, isn't it?

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.780
Yeah. 
A monster could break through it easily.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.710
So it's a total paper tiger?

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:27.850
Yeah, even though the gate is key to
stopping monsters from leaving the labyrinth.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:32.310
Everything about this dungeon city 
seems half-baked.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.820
Strong as an ox, as usual!

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.420
There's a powerful monster in there.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.530
Stay on your guard, all right?

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:53.370
Buy this, please.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.680
She underestimated her own strength

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.590
so the head was the only thing left, but...

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.980
The monster was deformed 
beyond recognition,

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:02.440
but Iris got off 
with a bump on the head.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:03.300
Th-This...

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.040
It's that monster!

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.010
The strong monster from yesterday...

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.460
Oh, is it really?

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:12.730
It definitely was the strongest one 
we ran into.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.920
H-How did you defeat it?

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:17.140
The normal way, I guess?

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:19.480
Though actually, 
I didn't get involved.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.850
The three of them did it.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:26.960
I can buy it, 
but you won't get paid till later.

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:30.040
The lord has to confirm it.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.780
I understand entirely.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:33.800
A moment, then, if you will...

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:45.120
<i>"If the report is to be believed, 
the three girls are total beasts."</i>

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:49.160
<i>"The boy appears to be a healer, 
and so didn't participate in the battle."</i>

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:49.980
<i>Hm?</i>

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.420
<i>What a curiously wrong conclusion 
to leap to...</i>

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.270
<i>Ah, well.</i>

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:59.400
I'm hungry!

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:02.650
Can I get gold for the rest of it right now?

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:05.240
"The rest"? You mean there's more?!

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:10.660
So they defeated that monster...

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:13.870
What an interesting party.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:16.330
Let's eat!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:20.740
You handled the combat today 
just fine without me.

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:24.060
We're really getting the hang 
of our teamwork!

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:27.330
Your enchantments, 
and my ranged attacks!

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:31.970
And once you've whittled the enemy down, 
I charge in!

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.230
Just try to rein it in a little, Iris.

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:35.590
Fine!

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.010
That was delicious!

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.620
I'm all full!

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:41.900
I could eat more, actually.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.950
<i>The lord's been spurred to action.</i>

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:51.980
<i>Perfect.</i>

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:54.420
<i>I'll unmask you.</i>

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:30.420
Wasn't Matty's healing today amazing?

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:32.290
Yeah, I wanna do the same thing!

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:33.500
- Scalpel! 
- Yes!

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.200
- Sweat! 
- Wipe, wipe!

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:37.320
My surgery skills are unrivaled!

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Episode 8 
The Strongest Sage Saves the City.</b>

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:39.890
Is that how I looked to you?
